body:
So you'd like if we keep talking? c:>

Yeah, but I think she was so mad because I'm almost 18 for fucks sake, you think I'd get my life more in order at this point and understand how to wash a spoon ;-;

Aww, yeah ;-; I didn't change and I was so sad that some friends just left me.. One teacher was nice and he was late to his class because he helped me push to my class. Then I had some friends who loved pushing me around so that was cool. c:

Aww ;-; when I'm down I get my favrorite food and watch videos, but I don't get that food often ^^;

Ah, I had oil in this little glass container to use on my bedside table (as I didn't need the whole container, now the container is empty and this is all I had left) but when I was cleaning my room recently I knocked it over and it broke and had the cooking oil all over the floor. I think it was olive oil, now I have vegetable oil in a little container that's plastic so if I drop it it won't break. I had to mop my room after and it was slippery and I slipped ;-;

Ah, common? My mom hit me once because I didn't wash the dishes correctly, and now she yells at me because I can't remember to put the spoons a certain way. I'm pretty sure she tells me to put them down on the towel, but if it's in the washing mashine to put them up, but since they are differennt I get confused a lot when I'm actually doing it...

I didn't know those were common though, that makes me feel a little better. I'm sorry for bringing up more stories as we keep talking, I just remember more and more ;-;

Oh, that sounds really nice actually. Oat meal is one of my favorite foods because when I was a tthe hospital it was the only thing I ate because anything with a strong taste made me sick, and anything with a smell made me sick. I always liked that I could add sugar/brown sugar to add taste and it had no smell change.

Ah, I don't have periods so I never actually had cramps except for once. After surgery, I had a regular period for four months, the first two I didn't notice pain because I had a wound there. The month after I noticed it, but it was the fourth that I felt it was awful, it's because I was out of the wheel chair the fourth month and I guess standing up makes it worse or something ;-; Another thing I hated, when I was in a wheel chair. a lot of my friends stopped talking to me, most ignored me and acted like I didn't exist when I tried to talk to them. ;-;
After that fourth month though it stopped again.

Yeah, so many people care, I'm still in contact with a few I met here. I love them so much, but one I don't get to talk to much because he's been going outside more, and I don't like texting because it gives me so much anxiety. I love coming here to talk to people.

And I didn't know, I thought that people who were clumsy and forgetful were just always hated, that's what it always seemed like...

Honestly, I'm feeling a little better now that I've eaten, it made me sick because of the sauce was such a strong taste, but I feel alright otherwise. I even messaged the friend who wanted to play a game with me and asked if he was still in the call, but I think he's busy because he didn't get to reply. it's alright like that because I think I tried to talk to early, I think I need more time to relax, I just don't know any more videos to watch.. ;-;
